{=============================================================================
  Centrifugal compressor design and similarity (methane)
  CoolSolve Library model CSL-0069 - variant of the main file
 -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Second part of the same exercise (ULiege, course Machines et systemes
  thermiques, MSTH 041012 4): diameter and rotation speed of a compressor of
  the same type, compressing 12000 m3/h of methane from 2 bar and 20 C to 3 bar.
  The flow factor phi and the enthalpy factor psi of the nominal point are the
  same as those of the air compressor of the main file, and the equations are
  the same; only the fluid (methane) and the nominal point change.

  Variant of centrifugal_compressor_design_similarity.eescode (see README.md):
  this is the continuation file of the exercise, imported as a separate
  runnable file, not a workaround of a CoolSolve gap. No equation was changed;
  the real-fluid methane (EES: lowercase `methane`) is the approximation kept
  active by the original, whose ideal-gas approximation (EES ideal-gas
  substance `CH4`) is left commented out, as in the original.

  Inputs : p_su, t_su, p_ex, V_dot_su (nominal point); phi, psi (flow and
           enthalpy factors of the nominal point)
  Outputs: D (impeller diameter), N, rpm, U (blade tip speed), A
  Units  : SI - temperatures in C, pressures in Pa, energies in J
  Source : ULiege course (J. Lebrun) - see README.md
=============================================================================}

"Nominal point and similarity factors of the methane compressor, as in the original"
p_su=2E5                   "suction pressure [Pa]"
t_su=20                    "suction temperature [C]"
p_ex=3E5                   "discharge pressure [Pa]"
V_dot_su=12000/3600        "suction volume flow rate [m3/s]"
phi=0.3                    "flow factor [-]"
psi=1.4                    "enthalpy factor [-]"
phi=V_dot_su/(U*A)         "flow factor"
U=pi*D*N                   "blade tip speed [m/s]"
A=pi*D^2/4                 "impeller inlet area [m2]"
rpm=N*60                   "rotation speed [rev/min]"
psi=DELTAh_s/(U^2/2)       "enthalpy factor"
DELTAh_s=h_exs-h_su        "isentropic enthalpy rise from suction to discharge [J/kg]"
"first approximation (probably sufficient): methane is assumed to be an ideal gas: CH4;
 second approximation: real gas - the active lines below, as in the original"
"h_su=ENTHALPY(CH4,T=T_su)"
h_su=ENTHALPY(methane,T=T_su, p=p_su)  "suction specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
"h_exs=ENTHALPY(CH4,s=s_su,p=p_ex)"
h_exs=ENTHALPY(methane,s=s_su,p=p_ex)  "isentropic discharge specific enthalpy [J/kg]"
"s_su=ENTROPY(CH4,T=T_su,P=P_su)"
s_su=ENTROPY(methane,T=T_su,P=P_su)     "suction specific entropy [J/kg-K]"